Found in a bug hunt, reproduced twice for priority and once for class,
and confirmed against the reference implementation.

Cmd/Pick.pm:153-160 sorts candidates with App::karr::Config->class_order
and ->priority_order -- fixed CLASS-METHOD tables (critical/high/medium/low,
expedite/fixed-date/standard/intangible). The board's own `priorities` and
`classes` lists are never consulted. Any name outside those tables hits the
`// 2` default, collapses into the medium/standard bucket, and the tie-break
becomes the task id.

Cmd/List.pm:291-305 does it correctly -- it reads $self->config->priorities
-- and its POD asserts the invariant "the top of a priority-sorted list is
the task App::karr::Cmd::Pick would hand out". That invariant is false on
any board with a custom list. kanban-md sorts pick candidates through
cfg.PriorityIndex / cfg.ClassIndex (internal/board/pick.go:74-90).

Reproduction, board with priorities: low, medium, high, critical, blocker

    $ karr create "merely critical" --priority critical   # id 1
    $ karr create "a blocker"       --priority blocker    # id 2
    $ karr list --sort priority --compact
    #2       backlog a blocker
    #1       backlog merely critical
    $ karr pick --claim tester
    Picked task 1: merely critical

With names the table knows nothing about (p3, p2, p1, p0), priority stops
influencing the pick entirely -- it hands out id 1, the least urgent.
Classes behave the same: on a board declaring classes [standard, expedite],
pick hands out the expedite card.

`karr context --sections in-progress` (Cmd/Context.pm:343) uses the same
table and orders critical above blocker for the same reason.

Note `priorities`/`classes` are not settable via `karr config set` (they are
read-only there) but ARE in %VIEW_KEY (Config.pm:796-799), so a custom list
arrives exactly the way a custom status list does: through `karr import` of
a kanban-md config.yml.

Cost: on any board imported from kanban-md with a non-default priority or
class list, every automated agent is handed the wrong work, silently and
consistently, while `karr list --sort priority` shows the correct order
right next to it.

Same class of bug as ticket #67 (hardcoded `done`), still standing for
priority and class.
