## Fix

Removed `App::karr::Config->priority_order` / `->class_order` (the hardcoded class methods that only knew the four default priorities and four default classes).

`karr pick` (`Cmd/Pick.pm`) now reads the board's own `priorities` and `classes` lists via `App::karr::Config->from_merged(effective_config)` and sorts by class index (lower = more urgent), then by priority index (higher = more urgent), then by task id -- matching kanban-md's `internal/board/pick.go:74-90`. The `// 2` fallback that hid the bug on unfamiliar names is gone.

`karr context --sections in-progress` (`Cmd/Context.pm:_pri_order`) now reads `$self->config->priorities` the same way; the briefing used to hang a `blocker` card in the middle of the list on a board that had it as the most urgent priority.

`Config.pm` lost the two helpers entirely rather than leaving them around. The only two callers were the bug sites, and leaving them invites a future caller to use the wrong one again.

`Task.pm` POD for `=attr priority` and `=attr class` now references the `Config/priorities` and `Config/classes` instance methods instead of the removed helpers.

Files: `lib/App/karr/Cmd/Pick.pm`, `lib/App/karr/Cmd/Context.pm`, `lib/App/karr/Config.pm`, `lib/App/karr/Task.pm`.

Test: `t/153-pick-custom-priorities.t` -- 6 subtests. Four of them (custom priorities, custom class set, class+priority combo, `context --sections in-progress`) fail on the old code with exactly the symptoms from the bug report and pass on the new one; the alphabetical / fully custom priorities subtest pins the exhaustive ordering so any future "fall back to a default" regression fails here; the default-board subtest is a sanity check.

`prove -l t/`: 144 files, 1033 tests, all green.
Moved to review. Config helpers removed; pick / context read the board own lists; 144 files / 1033 tests green.
